00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.960
I never expected that it would
come into use in this form.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.500
What about the functions that were
updated on the battlefield?

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.840
I have a backup of all the
combat records.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.570
What's going on?

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.880
So, in other words, we're
to be confined?

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.750
We have a situation on our hands,
so please understand.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.090
Must be with Special Services.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.280
Special Services?

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:05.460
Captain Gowa will be
allowed to go?

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:10.290
Yes. Gowa cannot allow Yushiro
to be arrested at this time.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.300
Is this the Gowa company
speaking?

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:17.760
No, I'm afraid it came across
the wrong way.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.540
I say this as his brother.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.630
Brother...

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.780
I want to go with them.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:30.480
You were assigned to them only as
part of the joint development.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.250
You're a civilian.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:37.920
Captain Gowa, I think you should
heed your brother's words.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.190
Even if the mass media
is buzzing about,

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:43.420
the timing of this quarantine
is too suspicious.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.000
A cover-up as part of a
misinformation campaign?

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.770
In any case, being a civilian and a
juvenile, Captain Gowa's presence

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:57.210
would be used by the opposition
and the media to censure us.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:03.250
Mr. Gowa, how soon will you be
able to have a car ready?

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.380
Now a permanent member of
the UN Security Council,
This latest overseas deployment,
without question,

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:07.820
Japan has important international
obligations she must live up to.
constituted military action, and
clearly is an unconstitutional act!

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.360
With this in mind, the action
taken by the Prime Minister
I would like to hear how our
Prime Minister explains

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.350
should be commended as
being courageous.
this arbitrary and audacious
decision he alone made.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:19.230
This overseas development did
not constitute military action.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:25.070
Regrettably, due to changes in
the local circumstances,

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.440
our forces were unintentionally
drawn into a conflict.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.710
That's a smoke screen!
our forces were unintentionally
drawn into a conflict.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:30.280
Was there an official request from
the UN Security Council?!

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.110
You're muddying the waters,
Prime Minister!

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.280
Yeah, yeah!
You're muddying the waters,
Prime Minister!

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.240
Yeah, yeah!

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.380
Are you ready to go, Yushiro?

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.790
See you again soon.

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.760
I'm sorry about leaving
by myself like this.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.900
What? Are you still thinking
about that?

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:56.870
That's right, for us this
is part of our job.

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:59.100
Don't let this bother you, Captain.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:04.440
To be honest, I still can't figure
you out, Captain.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:07.880
And I still want answers
for what happened.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.370
But...

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.650
But that was one hell of
a shot back there.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:23.160
We've got Special Services
to deal with.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:24.660
Time to go, everyone.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.730
What about the retrieval
of the sample?

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:27.930
Good.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.670
You didn't let Kiyotsugu
know, did you?

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:34.670
That's right, take Yushiro to the
Central Research Facility.

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:39.130
We need to start analyzing this
sample as soon as we can.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.080
Yes, I'll be back right away.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.280
It appears that the Department of
Defense's Internal Affairs office

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.980
is already moving.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:47.680
Yes, I'm well aware of it.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:57.030
Here are today's top headlines.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:59.300
Moments ago, a press conference
was held by the Prime Minister,

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.870
where Defense Minister Horiguchi
made the announcement

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:04.340
that the SSDF's experimental
company has returned to Japan,

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:09.340
arriving at Kagamigahara Airport
at 4:20 this morning.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:10.010
However...

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:10.680
However...
As I have made clear previously,
this overseas deployment

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.280
As I have made clear previously,
this overseas deployment

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:18.250
was conducted with peace keeping
activities in mind.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.740
This force was not...

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.020
Kazukiyo?

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.390
Yes.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:25.880
Come in.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.500
I've been told that Yushiro
has returned safely.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.930
And?

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:37.740
I'm thinking of sending him to the
Central Research Facility.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:40.240
Already? He's just arrived.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.540
I would like to have
your permission.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:46.070
I have no intention of inquiring
about affairs that are in the past.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:52.040
But I'll not sit by while avoidable
problems are allowed to slip by.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:07:02.060
I believed you when you said that
sending the TA's would allow us

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.860
to explore aspects of the TA's that
had not been pursued previously.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:07.390
But...

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:16.460
Your actions are like those of a
man painting himself into a corner.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:22.440
What was it in this expedition that
was worth taking such a risk?

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:26.820
Confirmation of the existence
of Belgistan TA's?

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.310
Simple impatience?

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:32.760
Amazing as they may seem, TA's
are nothing more than a unit

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:36.930
to be integrated in the vast
arsenal of a nation's military.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:40.870
Even if we are the pioneers
of their development,

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:44.700
the most we can hope for is
to increase our wealth as
merchants of death.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:49.840
Is it your ambition to
be a kugutsu?

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:56.280
I feel I am coming to understand
why a thousand years ago

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.420
the clan of the kai threw aside the
awesome power that was theirs

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:03.150
and allowed themselves
to become minimized

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:07.350
and forgotten by history.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.690
I have these dreams now.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.820
Dreams of Yushiro,
dreams of Kuya.

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:22.340
Dreams involving the two lives
I stole with my own hands.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:27.250
How many souls were sacrificed
for these foolish desires?!

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.550
We were able to survive
through the ages

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:34.080
because we threw aside
the boundless power.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.980
It's time we understood the full
implications of that fact.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:44.420
The karma of desire lays the seed
of its own destruction?

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:50.230
Here are the reports on the
Belgistan combat.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:09:00.370
Buddhists say that like a house
set ablaze by flames of desire,

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.620
suffering permeates all of life.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:08.180
But I believe it's an inferno
that burns one's self.

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:18.260
One hundred eighty seconds
to drop point.

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:19.830
Radar beacon confirmed.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.100
Confirming synchronization.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.500
Riding beam strength holding
at fifty-eight percent.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.940
Adjusting twenty-one points.
Rabastones three.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:27.040
Satellite feed, locked.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:30.640
Relative speed, minus twelve
points. All ready to go for drop.

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.130
Begin countdown.

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:39.240
Drop.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:56.630
Straying from target, less than
point zero eight percent.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:59.030
Recovery vehicle, head to
Point O as planned.

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:19.090
Act Two is about to begin, I see.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:22.390
This afternoon, in an unannounced
press conference,

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.660
they will make the TA's
existence public.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:28.170
We expect that a more formal
announcement will be made later,

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:31.330
and at that time it's likely you'll
be asked to operate the TA's.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.370
When will the investigative
sub-committee be convened?

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:37.310
Investigative sub-committee?
I don't follow you.

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:39.540
An investigative sub-committee for
this recent overseas deployment!

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:40.950
Were you under the impression

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.350
that you were being held because
of your role in the deployment?

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:47.250
What do you mean? Why
else would we be held?

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.650
You must only be acting
as if you don't know.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:53.720
It's to make sure that there are
no leaks made to the press.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.560
Plus...

00:10:56.560 --> 00:11:00.130
There is some bickering between
two factions who want to define

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.700
what the TA Project's primary
role should be.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.000
Primary role?

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.400
These are all rumors of
course, just rumors.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:08.510
But word is that TA's
were developed

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:12.240
with aims independent from the
needs of national defense.

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:17.650
And supposedly the person from
Gowa assigned to work with you

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:19.450
is referred to by them
as "the subject."

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:22.420
Corporations can be so
heartless at times.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:27.030
In any case, don't be careless in
how you present this to civilians.

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:31.460
There are reports that the Public
Prosecutors Office is after you.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:45.740
Mr. Nishida, Mr. Gowa was nice
enough to come today.

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:49.140
Mr. Gowa, let me introduce
you to Mr. Nishida.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.570
I'm Gowa.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:05.860
As you already know, Mr. Gowa
has rallied to our cause,

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:09.260
and has been generous enough to
promise us economic backing.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:15.670
The recent overseas expedition to
Belgistan was Mr. Gowa's idea.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:19.240
Since word of the
expedition got out,

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:21.510
the press is abuzz with arguments
regarding the SSDF.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:26.550
I believe it would be safe to say
that our original objective

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:29.590
of galvanizing public attention
on the issue of Japan's role

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:31.890
in the international community
has been accomplished.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.620
What about the
possibility of leaks?

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:37.530
We've been controlling
it very carefully.

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:41.430
For the moment, it's safe to say
that all is proceeding to plan.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:45.600
Then, we move into the second
phase of the plan now?

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:50.400
Yes, and that's why I've asked you
to come meet Mr. Nishida.

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:59.110
We believe that our actions must
be guided by a determined ideal.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:02.520
I realize you are well
aware of this,

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:06.390
but our job is to protect
the nation of Japan.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:10.600
But when we look back,

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:14.930
we are made to see an unsightly
nation corrupted by decadence.

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:19.570
There's no question Japan has
become much wealthier overall.

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:25.770
But isn't there more to life than
just securing material wellbeing?

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:28.510
The barren homeland overflows
with those who care not
about its state.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:31.120
Instead, their only interest is in
their insatiable desire to consume.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:34.920
Opportunism, irresponsibility,
and selfishness

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:37.680
constitute the skills necessary
to survive in this era.

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:43.330
This is something that's rubbed
off on me from Mr. Nishida.

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:47.570
Nevertheless, I've stated
sentiments common among us.

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:51.560
Spirits in search of
Japanese grace?

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:55.910
Virtues that once characterized
the Japanese people.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:59.640
A grace now lost.

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:03.580
But can we assume that such a
grace ever really existed?

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:14.990
I could not stand to watch the
Japanese people become corrupt.

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:20.160
That is why I repudiated my vision.

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:31.640
And yet, images of the corrupt
Japanese people

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:36.910
appear more vibrantly in my mind
than when my vision was intact.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:39.280
This must be the punishment

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:44.550
for my desire to avoid facing the
reality that surrounds me.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:52.500
You ask if there was a time when
Japanese grace was prevalent.

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:56.470
Unaware of their unsightly,
obese form,

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:59.900
the Japanese people slide down
the path of gradual necrosis.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:06.040
How can we be sure that isn't the
true nature of the Japanese?

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:21.530
The blade has been sharpened so
that it's thinner than expected.

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:25.960
I can no longer observe the details
of its blade signature pattern,

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:29.400
but I can still sense the cunning
aura of the sharp blade edge.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:35.060
Mr. Gowa, couldn't this be the true
essence of the Japanese?

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:39.840
Living by a transparent truth,
faithful to the homeland,

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:42.570
and appreciative of the beauty
of nature that surrounds one.

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:45.850
One who reveres self-discipline,

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:48.690
and considers selfishness to be
a disgraceful quality.

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:51.690
I believe this katana speaks
out to claim

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:57.320
that those principles are still
very much alive and viable.

00:15:58.130 --> 00:16:00.760
And therefore change
must be ushered in.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:05.600
Grace lost to time might yet be
restored to its former glory

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:07.610
as with this katana.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:12.810
If those who deeply love Japan
dedicated themselves to the task,

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:17.210
then the coarse surface and
rust might be lifted off.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:20.350
In other words we should rid
ourselves of our ochlocracy,

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:23.680
and return to the samurai
oligarchy of the past?

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:26.390
The vitality of democracy is rooted
in the principle behind it,

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:29.690
and not in the structure
established.

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:34.430
Just as a dictatorship is rooted
in principle, not structure.

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:39.540
The only instance in this nation

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:44.410
where reform tried to alleviate
the suffering of the masses

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:46.780
and establish order was when
the samurai class rose up.

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:50.480
And that's why a military
dictatorship is necessary.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:53.250
Only as a necessary evil.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:56.850
But even a necessary evil

00:16:56.850 --> 00:17:01.850
leads to a path of profiteering and
bribery if power is unchallenged.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:08.930
People become swept up in
power without realizing it.

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:13.100
The concentration of power
shall only last three years.

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:16.010
In three years time,

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:20.380
a political body based on ideals
and resolve must be established,

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:23.850
and then we will step aside and
allow the masses to judge us.

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:28.680
And what if success cannot be
secured within three years?

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:30.650
What if?

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:33.220
The position of the heavens,
favorable geo-politics,

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:34.710
and the accord of the people...

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:39.590
If any one of these is missing, no
true revolution can come about.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:44.760
We must risk everything
at that moment.

00:17:48.070 --> 00:17:53.010
Mr. Gowa, I know that
not all of us here

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.780
have securing political power over
Japan as our primary objective.

00:17:55.780 --> 00:18:01.580
But I believe we're united in our
desire to jar Japan in some way.

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:06.010
Japanese swords are
indeed graceful,

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:09.390
but in the end they are nothing
more than instruments to kill.

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:13.120
No, you should know that's not all.

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:17.600
In the past, the Japanese people
worshipped their swords as gods,

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:21.370
hoping that they would be granted
the power to defeat the wicked.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.910
Just as with the Gasaraki!

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:54.570
Are you sure about this?

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:57.370
How can I just stand around after
being told what we now know?

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:00.610
But you'll be punished
if they find out!

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:02.080
That's never stopped me.

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:06.880
Excuse me...

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:10.790
I'm awfully sorry, but I have
a favor I need to ask.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:11.760
Would you mind?

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:12.290
Yes?
Would you mind?

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:12.760
Yes?

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:17.160
Well you see, I really need
to borrow a car...

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:29.970
Intrusion point is set
at 02-11-855.

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:31.570
Your path will be through Zone C.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:38.180
F-2 is to recover the XF-4
fragment taken by them.

00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:41.590
F-1 is to intrude into
point 03-25-512,

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:44.360
and gather any and all intelligence
regarding Gowa's invitator.

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:46.980
You are instructed to avoid
hostilities as best as you can.

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:51.020
F-1, F-2, ready.

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:22.160
All right, now we can calculate a
path to the fragment's location,

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:24.180
and determine how to hack
into their server.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:43.870
Who is it?

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:16.980
Dead?!

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:19.070
Over eight years ago?

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:45.500
You're...

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.570
Miharu!

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:53.180
Gowa... Yushiro...

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.080
I searched through the data
pertaining to you,

00:21:57.050 --> 00:22:01.650
only to find that Yushiro Gowa
died eight years ago.

00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:17.600
I died?

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:20.100
Eight years ago?

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:33.480
Hark

00:22:34.640 --> 00:22:39.930
It's time I journey

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:50.600
Break apart my heart

00:22:50.770 --> 00:22:57.130
For crimson sadness

00:22:57.460 --> 00:23:04.640
Pours out from it

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:08.560
I can only, oh

00:23:08.670 --> 00:23:11.750
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:11.840 --> 00:23:17.360
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:36.460
I can only, oh

00:23:36.550 --> 00:23:39.610
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:44.810
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:46.340 --> 00:23:52.790
I beg you, be by my side

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:02.780
I died?

00:24:02.780 --> 00:24:04.270
Over eight years ago?

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.640
Then who am I?

00:24:07.420 --> 00:24:09.520
Who can reveal the truth to me?

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:11.180
Where do I need to go to
find out the truth?

00:24:11.790 --> 00:24:14.120
In the storehouse where the old
Gowa house in Kinashi was?

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:16.560
Stored there in the dark

00:24:16.560 --> 00:24:19.430
Patiently hibernating,
the ancient lives

00:24:19.430 --> 00:24:22.490
Passion stagnates there in the
deep darkness of the storehouse

00:24:23.330 --> 00:24:26.960
Who are you, standing in the
shadows, looking out at me?
